works: {child} keeps at it, and one evening plays a whole tune for {N} without a mistake; the case never goes back in the wardrobe.
works: A year on, {child} is better than {N} ever was, and {N} is prouder of that than of anything {N} played.
fails: Three weeks in, {child} loses interest, and the instrument goes back in its case.
fails: {N} pushes too hard, the lessons turn into rows, and {child} stops wanting to play at all.
